<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Christian Coalition parties split.</title>
<headline>NZ Christian Coalition parties split.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Christian Democrats are leaving the Christian Coalition, the New Zealand Press Association reported on Monday.</p>
<p>It quoted the New Zealand Christian newspaper Challenge Weekly as saying that a public meeting was held on April 26, where Democrats Graeme Lee and Annetta Moran said their party had different objectives to the Christian Heritage party and there was no reason to continue the coalition.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
